* s1manual.scheme
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* dash translation of Stata's s1manual scheme.
*
* Source Stata scheme file : /Applications/StataNow/ado/base/s/scheme-s1manual.scheme
* Stata version            : StataNow 19.5 (MP), born 12 Aug 2026
* Stata #include chain     : s2color -> s1color -> s1mono -> s1manual
* Translated on            : 22sep2026
* Derived from             : test/fixtures/scheme_truth.json, generated by
*                            scripts/extract_scheme_truth.py from Stata's own
*                            scheme-*.scheme and style/*.style files.
*
* Every colour below is a RESOLVED #rrggbb value, not a Stata colour name
* (a %NN suffix is Stata's opacity, kept as the scheme writes it), and
* every p#stub is spelled out p1..p15 because SchemeParser reads by exact
* key with no fallback.  The provenance block at the end says, for every
* directive, which Stata directive it was transcribed from or which
* fallback rule inferred it.
*
* Re-extract and re-check this file whenever Stata is upgraded: the header
* above is only true as of the version and date recorded in it.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

label "s1 manual - mono"

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Directives, written 22sep2026 by scripts/extract_scheme_truth.py (WP-17)
* from test/fixtures/scheme_truth.json.  Every value is resolved from
* Stata's own #include chain and style files (chain:
* s2color -> s1color -> s1mono -> s1manual); colours are pre-resolved #rrggbb, a %NN
* suffix being Stata's opacity kept as written; every p#stub is spelled
* out p1..p15.  Re-running the script re-checks every directive here.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

* Background and region colours.
color background   #ffffff
color plotregion   #ffffff
color legend       #ffffff
color legend_line  #000000
color major_grid   #e0e0e0
color minor_grid   #505050
color heading      #000000
color axisline     #000000

* Per-plot colour cycle p# (Stata's p#stub -> pstub -> p# -> p chain, flattened).
color p1   #606060
color p2   #a0a0a0
color p3   #808080
color p4   #404040
color p5   #000000
color p6   #c0c0c0
color p7   #202020
color p8   #707070
color p9   #909090
color p10  #b0b0b0
color p11  #d0d0d0
color p12  #505050
color p13  #303030
color p14  #c0c0c0
color p15  #505050

* Per-plot colour cycle p#line (Stata's p#stub -> pstub -> p# -> p chain, flattened).
color p1line   #000000
color p2line   #000000
color p3line   #000000
color p4line   #000000
color p5line   #000000
color p6line   #000000
color p7line   #000000
color p8line   #000000
color p9line   #000000
color p10line  #000000
color p11line  #000000
color p12line  #000000
color p13line  #000000
color p14line  #000000
color p15line  #000000

* Per-plot colour cycle p#bar (Stata's p#stub -> pstub -> p# -> p chain, flattened).
color p1bar   #606060
color p2bar   #a0a0a0
color p3bar   #808080
color p4bar   #404040
color p5bar   #000000
color p6bar   #c0c0c0
color p7bar   #202020
color p8bar   #707070
color p9bar   #909090
color p10bar  #b0b0b0
color p11bar  #d0d0d0
color p12bar  #505050
color p13bar  #303030
color p14bar  #c0c0c0
color p15bar  #505050

* Per-plot colour cycle p#mark (Stata's p#stub -> pstub -> p# -> p chain, flattened).
color p1mark   #606060
color p2mark   #a0a0a0
color p3mark   #808080
color p4mark   #404040
color p5mark   #000000
color p6mark   #c0c0c0
color p7mark   #202020
color p8mark   #707070
color p9mark   #909090
